SUMMARY:What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Nov 5 thru Nov 11**\nUpcoming **music
  events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n(U
 pdates on Thurs morning)\n.\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & market 
 events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of
 -events\n.\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.l
 ibcal.com/\n.\n**Every Friday\; Nov 6**\nCountry Dance Lesson - Style Vari
 es\n7-8pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Hendersonville NC 287
 92\nCost: $5 per person.\n.\n**Nov 5 thru Dec 20\;** Event Times: 2:00 PM 
 & 7:30 PM\; $$$\nA Flat Rock Playhouse Christmas Show – 10th Anniversary
  Special\nhis year’s festivities are stuffed fuller than Santa’s sleig
 h with the songs you can’t wait to hear — the holiday hits and beloved
  carols you ask for every year\, delivered with fa-la-la flair and show-st
 opping shine.\nJoin us for a spectacular celebration that is wrapped in jo
 y\, tied with tradition\, and topped with a bow of pure Playhouse magic.\n
 Flat Rock Playhouse\; 2661 Greenville Hwy\, Leiman Mainstage\nhttps://visi
 thendersonvillenc.org/event/a-flat-rock-playhouse-christmas-show-10th-anni
 versary-special/2026-12-06\nhttps://purchase.flatrockplayhouse.org/overvie
 w/4120\n.\n**November 6 - November 18**\nOur Town – An Art Exhibition\na
 t Art MoB Studios\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/our-town-an-art
 -exhibition-celebrating-henderson-county\nhttps://www.artmobstudios.com/\n
 .\n**November 6\;** 4:00 pm - 7:00 pm\nKanuga Station Open House and Pop-u
 p Market\nTour Hendersonville’s newest coworking space and shop local ve
 ndors from Blue Ridge Artisan Market. Bring a business card to enter drawi
 ngs for a free one-month membership and a one-week pass. Free and open to 
 the public.\n512 Kanuga Road Hendersonville\nhttps://blueridgeartisanmarke
 t.com/\n.\n**November 6** @ 6:00 pm - 8:00 pm\; Free\nIn Good Company Nov 
 6 – Opening Reception\nIn Good Company brings together familiar work by 
 artists who’ve exhibited at Studio 116 and new work by artists we’re w
 elcoming for the first time.\nhttps://www.studio116nc.com/\n.\n**November 
 7** @ 9:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\n**Holiday Craft Fair & Bake Sale in Etowah
  NC**\nhosted by Etowah United Methodist Church. Now celebrating its 42nd 
 year\, this beloved community tradition offers a festive day of handmade g
 ifts\, baked goods\, and holiday cheer — all while supporting local miss
 ions.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/holiday-craft-fair\n**.**\n
 **SATURDAY\, NOVEMBER 7**\nJ & M FARMS \\* The Caribbean Cowboys \\* music
  6:00 – 9:00\n.\n**Sunday\, Nov 8**\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club 
 Tea Dance - Attire: Dress to impress\n3-5:30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhode
 s Veterans Center\, 900 North Main St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n3pm - Dan
 ce Lesson.\nAmple parking at the front entry of the building\, take the el
 evator or stairs to the upper level. Parking is limited at the rear entran
 ce\, both front and back doors will be unlocked. 3-5:30pm –\nOur dances 
 are open to the public and everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom Dancing to 
 the music of DJ Gary Bills who plays a variety of dance tunes including Sw
 ing (East & West Coast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. The
 re is also a dance mixer Cost: $5 per person at door.\n.\n**November 8** @
  12:00 pm - 5:00 pm\nEarly-Bird Holiday Market\nJoin at Packa’s Place an
 d get your holiday shopping done early. There will be delicious baked good
 s\, food from Smokee’s wood fired pizza\, 20 local makers and artisans a
 nd live music from 12-5pm!\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/early-
 bird-holiday-market\n\,\n**November 9** @ 6:30 pm - 7:30 pm\; $100\nBellyd
 ance Foundations 4-Week New Choreography Series\nDiscover Your Rhythm with
  my New 4-Week Bellydance Choreography series. Unleash your inner rhythm\,
  build core strength\, and express yourself through the art of bellydance!
  Designed specifically for beginners\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/ev
 ent/bellydance-foundations-4-week-new-choreography-series/2026-11-09\n\n**
 Tuesday\, November 10**\nDancing the Night Away – Line dancing\, Swing\,
  Ballroom & More (Free Event)\n6-8pm\, First United Methodist Church\, 204
  6th Avenue\, Hendersonville NC 28739\nThe night will start with a Line Da
 nce Lesson followed by open dancing.\nThey will have free refreshments and
  tables and chairs will be set up. All you need is your dancing shoes.\nPa
 rking is in the rear of the church and enter through the double doors. For
  more information text Michael Bannon at 828-458-7153.\n.\n**Every Wednesd
 ay\, Nov 11**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, S
 outhern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n.\n**Every W
 ednesday\, Nov 11th**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up) (Each Wedne
 sday)\n7-10pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite 101\, Hende
 rsonville NC 28792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - Beginner Less
 on. 8-10pm - Social Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our incredible inst
 ructor lineup: Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMissy Lindsey\
 , Rachel Harris\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all bringing fre
 sh energy and\nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of community DJs k
 eeping the vibes high and the floor full all night\nlong. No outside drink
 s (including water bottles) - water station available. Outside food welcom
 e. Dress is\ncasual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking next to the v
 enue & street parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing host venue by g
 rabbing a drink or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance nights thriving!
 \nPricing: $10 lesson & social\, $5 social only\n.\n\nThese are NOT hosted
  events and are posted for informational purposes only. Please make person
 al arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend 
 and host one of these events\, I will post the event as an individual happ
 ening. Hosting only requires being focal point for others and making intro
 ductions. Simple!!
