SUMMARY:Rumbling Bald Trail\; a Saunter 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nThe Rumbling Bald Trail is a loop trail tha
 t meanders through a beautiful hardwood forest along the south face of Rum
 bling Bald Mountain\, revealing huge boulder fields and the base of the cl
 iff areas. These are the cliffs that can be seen from Lake Lure.\nRemember
  - hikes led by Gordie tend to have pleasant surprises.\nDifficulty: Moder
 ate: well developed trail with undulating gradual climbs w natural trail s
 urface. Some stone stairs. Some steep sections.\nDue to recent events\, Bi
 gfoot discussions are no longer permitted.\nWe are the Sloth Hike Team of 
 WNC: “We will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the 
 ‘real’ hike groups don’t !!\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4
 EK2vt4**\n**Details:**\nDistance: 2.5 mile Loop\; Accum ascent: 500ft\; Pa
 ce: **1.5mph**\nDrive time: 3/4hr/35 miles (one way)\nGoogle map = “Rumb
 ling Bald Access\, Lake Lure\, NC”\nReturn Not earlier than: 3.00 PM\n**
 Optional: Lunch in Chimney Rock (add 1.5 hrs)**\nCarpool contributions app
 reciated. $4.00 suggested\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event 
 is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs.
  Well trained dogs **(you don’t have to yell)** can be 'off-leash'. 'On 
 leash' in vicinity of other hike groups. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Larg
 e dogs will drive themselves.\nWeather Check: Lake Lure\, NC\nWAITLISTED P
 EOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 3.5 driver(s) (=
 14ppl)\nWe suggest open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own h
 ealth status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or 
 the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringi
 ng your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessa
 nt prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair.\nAll hikes are at you
 r own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment
 .\n**Waiver:** There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. E
 ach participant\, member\, and guest By signing up to attend this event\, 
 agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendersonville Fun Friend
 s\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, il
 lness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating in this act
 ivity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participa
 nt further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\
 , to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionall
 y separated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any 
 images collected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\
 ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 82
 8.393.0297 ( text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N
 05/albums**
